  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-30T09:51:56.648Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "DevUpdate on 29 Sep 2022 https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-29-september-2022/14026 says ...\n> “Show Avatar” and “Hide Avatar” player moderations will be saved locally instead of saved on the server\n> Show and Hide Avatar player moderations ... can be cleared if you delete all VRChat local data\nSeriously, I don't want my hide avatar to disappear that easily.\nI have been using hide avatar mainly in public instances as a marker that someone is a person to watch out for who is not worth blocking, but tends to have an offensive avatar or say or do things that are offensive (but often interesting enough to engage with from a distance).\nI suspect that there are other users who have used this feature under the assumption that it will be persistent on the server.\nI would like to see an option to exclude the show / hide avatar information when deleting local data.",
